.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH trimsec 1  "trimsec 5.1.1" 
.SH NAME
trimsec
.SH SYNOPSIS
ts [ARGS | COMMAND]
.br
Usage:
.br
ts [ARGS]:
.br
ts 1h24m 2h 1.25x
.br
# trim mode (implicit combination)
.br
ts 1h24m+2h+1m 1.25x
.br
# trim mode (explicit combination)
.br
ts 1h24m 1.25x <URL> 2h30m 1.25x ...
.br
# arbitrary arguments
.br
ts 1h24m
.br
# fit\-check (remaining time until midnight as budget)
.br
ts 1h24m+20m+30m b12h
.br
# explicit combination and explicit budget
.br
ts 1h24m 2h
.br
# second duration argument is interpreted as the budget
.br
ts <URL> 3h20m <URL> ...
.br
# arbitrary arguments
.br
ts <URL> 1h13m1.5s <URL> ... b12h
.br
# explicit 12h budget via \*(Aqb\*(Aq prefix
.br
ts \-clip 1.5x
.br
# reads duration/URL directly from system clipboard
.br
ts [COMMAND]:
.br
See commands below.
.br
Argument Syntax:
.br
<DURATION>
.br
e.g. 1h24m, 2h30m, 1m13.5s
.br
<SPEED>
.br
e.g. 1.25x
.br
<BUDGET>
.br
b<DURATION>
.br
e.g. b12h
.br
<COMBINATION>
.br
<DURATION>+<DURATION>+...
.br
e.g. 1h24m+20m+30m
.br
<URL>
.br
Any YouTube URL (videos/music/Shorts).
.br
<PLAYLIST>
.br
A YouTube playlist URL.
.br
\-clip
.br
Reads duration or URL directly from system clipboard.
.br
Argument Interpretation:
.br
\- Adjacent duration arguments are implicitly combined when used in
.br
trim mode.
.br
ts 1h24m 2h 1.25x
.br
=> (1h24m + 2h) at 1.25x
.br
\- Durations may be explicitly combined with \*(Aq+\*(Aq.
.br
ts 1h24m+2h+1m 1.25x
.br
=> (1h24m + 2h + 1m) at 1.25x
.br
\- A standalone second duration argument is interpreted as the budget
.br
when the command is in fit\-check mode.
.br
ts 1h24m 2h
.br
=> check 1h24m against a 2h budget
.br
\- A budget prefixed with \*(Aqb\*(Aq explicitly specifies the budget.
.br
ts 1h24m+20m+30m b12h
.br
=> check (1h24m + 20m + 30m) against a 12h budget
.br
\- If no budget is specified, fit\-check uses the remaining time until
.br
midnight as the budget.
.br
\- A <SPEED> argument applies to the duration/combination immediately
.br
preceding it.
.br
Specific Arg\-Syntax:
.br
max:<n>::<PLAYLIST>
.br
Only traverse the first n items in a YouTube playlist.
.br
Example:
.br
max:10::https://youtube.com/playlist?list=...
.br
Keyword Arguments:
.br
1. Color mode:
.br
\-\-color <ColorMode>
.br
e.g. \-\-color auto
.br
or:
.br
\-\-color=<ColorMode>
.br
e.g. \-\-color=auto
.br
Modes:
.br
always
.br
auto
.br
never
.br
Keyword arguments may appear anywhere in the argument list.
.br
Commands:
.br
See commands below.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
trimsec\-path(1)
Shows the path of the configuration file
.TP
trimsec\-list(1)
Lists all entries in a YouTube playlist
.TP
trimsec\-key(1)
Command group for managing the Google Cloud Console API key
.TP
trimsec\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH VERSION
v5.1.1
